**Goal:** Close the three concrete gaps surfaced by the 2026-06-21 Ebbinghaus + search audit — untested decay constants, the documented-but-missing access-reinforcement writeback toggle, and the absent PageRank graph signal — without adding any external dependency.

**Architecture:** The `builder_knowledge` crate already ships a query-time Ebbinghaus decay model (`tag_indexer.rs::memory_strength`) multiplied into a 3-channel RRF hybrid search (BM25 + FNV-hash embedding + graph BFS). This plan adds (1) golden regression tests pinning the decay math, (2) an opt-in, default-off `BUILDER_KNOWLEDGE_MEMORY_WRITEBACK` env gate that wires the existing `MemoryConsolidator::record_access` into the read path so code matches the completion report, and (3) a pure-Rust power-iteration PageRank precomputed at graph-build time and added as a bounded bonus into the fused base score.

**Tech Stack:** Rust (edition per workspace), `chrono`, `anyhow`, `regex`, `serde`; test runner `cargo test -p builder_knowledge`. No new crates.

## Global Constraints

- **No external model · no ONNX · no GPU · no new third-party crate · CPU-only · pure-Rust, local-first.** (Honors `AGENTS.md` dependency gate and the completion report's constraints.)
- **Single source of truth for decay constants is `tag_indexer.rs`** — tests assert against it; do not fork the numbers elsewhere.
- **Retrieval stays read-only by default.** Any disk mutation on the read path must be behind an explicit, default-off env flag, mirroring the existing `BUILDER_KNOWLEDGE_GC` opt-in precedent. Unset flag ⇒ zero disk writes, ranking unchanged.
- **No behavior regression:** `cargo test -p builder_knowledge` must stay green (baseline 36 passing) after every task.
- **Backwards-compatible ranking:** PageRank enters as an additive, weight-bounded bonus; with an empty/linkless graph the bonus is 0 and existing rankings are unchanged.

